Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:00.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.90,0:00:03.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Population: eight billion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.90,0:00:07.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Now… imagine every one of them, gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.40,0:00:08.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Hour one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.40,0:00:11.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The power plants run on, with no one left to feed them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.70,0:00:15.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}One by one… the lights go out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.10,0:00:16.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Hour thirty-six.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.60,0:00:20.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Beneath New York, seven hundred and fifty pumps have stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.70,0:00:22.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The subway floods.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.80,0:00:23.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Year twenty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.90,0:00:25.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Roots split the asphalt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.60,0:00:28.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Trees rise through the streets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.90,0:00:30.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Year three hundred.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.20,0:00:33.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}With no one to paint it, the Eiffel Tower rusts…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.40,0:00:35.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and falls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.30,0:00:36.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Year five hundred.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.60,0:00:39.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Forests have taken back our cities.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.80,0:00:42.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}But one thing we made will outlast us all…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.90,0:00:43.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Plastic.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.90,0:00:47.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Still here, thousands of years from now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.50,0:00:51.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}So tell me… would Earth even miss us?
